LadrunoSANISAND tag 1: p_residual = 0 (default, cohesionless), pRe = 0 (default, OFF: G, K ~ sqrt(max(p, p_min)/P_atm), no stiffness floor), p_min = 0.0101 (user), honorTolR = 0 (INERT: IntScheme 129 = SAS-ME uses TolR = 0.0001 as its substep tolerance), TanType = 1 (continuum mCep), maxSubsteps = 2000 (ModifiedEuler FAILS the update past this many substeps, so the step can be cut), reversalTol 1e-10 (undoes integrate()'s mAlpha_in loading-reversal reset when ||eps - eps_n|| falls below this, i.e. treats it as round-off noise), reversalRel 0.05 (SECOND threshold = reversalRel * ||last committed d_eps||; a hold's noise tracks the solver tolerance, not round-off, so the absolute test alone under-catches it); reversal test skipped on dt == 0 (ops_Dt, unconditionally -- a hold has no loading to test for a reversal in); hold-skip commits counted in implexGuards[5] [D5b: D_factor sigmoid non-dimensionalised in vanilla (PR-2), an exact no-op at P_atm = 101; D5a: whether it should exist at all once the residual pressure is zero is still OPEN]
LadrunoSANISAND tag 1: -flipAlphaIn init (flip: alpha_in := alpha (init, the DEFAULT since WP-112: deterministic at every point, independent of round-off and of the MKL thread count)), -implexFlipAbsorb OFF (the DEFAULT: the flip commits nothing beyond mElastFlag's own effect on the next real step -- required for the ADR-92 gate-5 -implex ON-vs-OFF byte-identity on a zero-free-DOF deck)
LadrunoSANISAND tag 1: IntScheme 129 = SAS-ME (WP-129): substep error on stress, alpha and fabric <= TolR = 0.0001 (always honoured; ~1e-4 is ModifiedEuler's scale), sigma_ref = 1 (default P_atm/101 = 1 kPa at P_atm 101), alpha_in reseat (DEFAULT), rho_alpha: flow bound 1 + 0.1, entry refusal above 1 + 2 (outside: reject, refuse at dT_min); TanType 1 and 2 both return the continuum tangent at the end state. Refusals reach the element as -33086; census: the `sasStats` response.
